import Mathlib

/-!
# Exact localized modes at Pluecker sign walls (Paper C pillar 3 witness)

Overnight publication run 2026-07-11, Fable lane F2.  All data below was
generated by exact rational arithmetic (sympy oracle, scratchpad
`wall_mode_exact.py`) and verified symbolically before submission; every
proof is pure literal arithmetic with no search.

Physics.  `wallWalk` is the 1+1 split-step Dirac walk on an 8-site ring
whose real Pluecker mass field carries the 3-4-5 coin (cos = 4/5,
sin = 3/5) with a SIGN WALL between sites 3|4 and 7|0 (the field is
+m on sites 0-3 and -m on sites 4-7; the sign change is the collinearity
crossing of the underlying spinor pair field, `wallField` below).
`constWalk` is the zero-wall control (constant +m).

Results to prove:
* T1/T2: the explicit vectors `modePlus`/`modeMinus` are EXACT eigenvectors
  of `wallWalk` with eigenvalues `+1` and `-1` - Jackiw-Rebbi-type bound
  states pinned at finite size with rational data;
* T3: `modePlus` is localized at the 3|4 wall: its site probability at
  sites 3 and 4 equals `256/5`, while at the antipodal sites 0 and 7 it
  equals `1` (a factor `256/5` concentration);
* T4: the zero-wall control has NO `+1` or `-1` eigenvector: explicit
  two-sided inverse certificates `certMinus`/`certPlus` for
  `constWalk -+ 1`;
* T5: the wall sign profile is the Pluecker coordinate of an explicit
  primitive spinor pair field (derivation, not assignment).

Prohibited weakenings: do not replace exact eigenvector identities by
spectral approximations; do not drop the zero-wall control; do not change
any literal.  Suggested proof route: `Matrix.mulVec` / matrix product
unfolding via `Fin.sum_univ_succ` (or `Finset.sum_fin_eq_sum_range`) then
`Complex.ext_iff` + `norm_num` entrywise; `funext i; fin_cases i` to split
the sixteen coordinates.
-/

noncomputable section

